# Live scanner notes

When the user reports a live Slack miss, a false alert, late relay, wrong
sw1/sw2/FVG text, or a protocol idea from a live session, append a dated
block to `live/LIVE_SCANNER_NOTES.md` (newest first, below the open
queue). Use the template in that file. Update the open queue if the
note is a repeating pattern.

**Stop there.** Nothing written in that log changes a version that is
open/live now (`smt_scanner_v8_7.py`, `smt_scanner_v8_8.py`,
`smt_scanner_v8_10.py`) or any later live scanner. Do not edit those
files, retune thresholds, push a version, or add a new scanner because
a note was logged.

A version change, patch, push, or new protocol file happens only when
the user **explicitly names the version and asks for the change**, and
the change is **directly verified** before it is treated as done.
`Wanted change` and open-queue rows are notes, not work orders.
Threshold retunes to recover one live print must be flagged in that
explicit request first.
